## Context

Appliquer le contrat 0716 au JETP sénégalais depuis la déclaration de juin
2023 jusqu'à la date de collecte. Le Plan d'investissement et ses annexes,
publiés après le lancement, rendent obsolète toute photographie arrêtée à
2024. Couvrir ministère, IPG, bailleurs, Senelec, projets de renouvelables,
réseau, accès et articulation avec les nouveaux hydrocarbures.

## Test

Le contrôle de couverture échoue sans verdict pour le ministère, IPG, AFD,
KfW, UE, Royaume-Uni, Canada, banques multilatérales et Senelec. Chaque projet
du Plan d'investissement et de ses annexes doit avoir une identité stable,
une source et un statut ; le chiffre AFD-Senelec de 670 M€ reste exclu tant
qu'une source primaire ne le confirme.

## Exit criteria

- [x] Déclaration, Plan d'investissement et annexes collectés
- [ ] Chaque projet du plan est relié à ses pages bailleur/opérateur
- [x] Financement, état physique et dépendance hydrocarbures restent distincts
- [x] L'absence de publication annuelle est enregistrée comme donnée
- [x] Contrôle de couverture Sénégal passe


## Recovery and review evidence (13 September 2026)

Recovery checkpoint `8917149c` preserves the complete original archive and
167 restored canonical documents. The follow-up adds 28 collected documents;
all 195 canonical documents and the original archive were read back from the
DVC remote and checked by MD5 and SHA-256. See
`docs/jetp-recovery-2026-09-13.md`.

The 49 plan lines resolve to 43 project/programme records. QW1 matches
submission 15; PUELEC remains distinct from its 600-village component. The
records are not additive assets. Red commit `c7995fab` specifies these scope
boundaries and separates proposed finance from physical implementation.
`tests/test_jetp_senegal_project_coverage.py` checks every dated verdict,
confirmed direct-source links, unresolved routes, and exclusion of EUR 670m.

The documentary pass is complete: 18 records have direct corroboration,
21 remain central-only after follow-up, and four ASER routes are blocked.
The literal direct-page exit criterion remains open for those 25 records;
this is not a claim that all projects have independently confirmed progress.
`project-coverage.csv`, `project-source-links.csv`, and `dry-searches.csv`
record the routes and limitations. Finance, physical status and hydrocarbon
dependence have separate fields/events, including explicit unknowns.

Validation: 88 JETP tests passed; check-fast passed (25 package checks plus
1,520 tests), and lint passed (332 tests). The full suite initially reported
2,408 passed and eight failures caused by absent non-JETP corpus files in the
fresh worktree. After copying existing local corpus outputs, both affected
modules passed (62 passed, 18 skipped). No production-code fix was needed.


## Resumed completion pass

First test: Diass must have the operator-reported 31 March 2026 construction
launch, without a commissioning inference; CETUD BioGNV must resolve to the
IFC advisory project 609428, without converting advisory approval into plant
capital finance. An ASER source failure must remain distinct from evidence
that the submitted project is absent. All 43 records must appear in the final
review with source locators and remaining verification limits.

Follow the 25 unresolved identities using Annex 8 promoter descriptions,
operator publications and funder project databases. Recheck the previously
collected projects for newer milestones. Archive public documents and preserve
failed attempts. Close the documentary work with a per-project evidence report;
do not close a literal direct-source criterion by relabelling central evidence.


## Resumed pass result and criterion evidence

- Central documents: preserved hashes and recovery evidence in `8917149c` and
  `2438dbf4`, `docs/jetp-recovery-2026-09-13.md`.
- Direct project pages: **MISSING for 24 identities**. The new IFC BioGNV
  disclosure resolves one previous central-only verdict. Current counts are
  19 collected, 20 central_only, four blocked. No criterion was relaxed.
- Distinct finance/physical/hydrocarbon observations: `2438dbf4` adds 32 plan
  needs/allocations and two dated funding observations, records Diass launch
  and BioGNV advisory preparation, and preserves explicit unknowns.
  Evidence: `test_diass_groundbreaking_is_dated_without_claiming_commissioning`
  and `test_biognv_advisory_approval_is_not_plant_capital_finance`.
- Annual publication absence: earlier authority coverage remains unchanged;
  a project/operator update is not relabelled a JETP annual report.
- Coverage: all 43 identities have documented verdicts and implementation
  baselines; `test_every_senegal_project_has_a_terminal_followup_verdict` and
  `test_senegal_completion_report_covers_every_project_and_its_limits` pass.

Full project review: `docs/jetp-senegal-review-2026-09-13.md`. Remaining source
requests are prioritised there. The public documentary pass and extraction are
complete, but a direct-source-complete claim or merge approval is not justified.

Validation on the resumed data: 91 JETP tests; check-fast 25 package checks plus
1526 passed/7 skipped; lint 332 passed/10 skipped; full make check 2455 passed/
47 skipped in 214 seconds. No failures. Fifteen new documents backed up, and
all 210 canonical objects plus the original recovery archive verified by remote
readback (MD5 and SHA-256); 253 manifest rows checked. No independent PR review
yet. Keep the draft PR and literal direct-source criterion open.

## Deeper case investigation

First test: ARTELIA metadata must corroborate QW1 separately from the provisional
Ouarkhokh/Champions Nationaux join. Environmental studies and matching sites
must not create a capital-finance observation. Preserve all 43 identities.
Deliver a cited case note connecting financial design, preparation evidence,
local impacts and the installed-capacity target, with unresolved joins explicit.

Deeper-pass evidence: red test commit `9390aed6`; source links distinguish
ARTELIA site corroboration from the provisional Ouarkhokh/QW2 join. The case
note calculates proposed equity/debt shares, records the earlier Huawei MoU
reference and separates capacity, generation and emissions baselines. The
24 unresolved direct identities remain open. No merge approval is asserted.

## Merge review corrections

The first review found three defects not caught by the prior suite.
`f605b4c9` and `e9c754ef` add failing regression tests; `102cdacc` preserves
reviewed Senegal reconciliation on stable source rows and rejects wrong PDF
hashes before parsing; `18ae2724` stops inferring financial approval from
physical progress and corrects 14 ZAF observations to announced. Amounts and
source physical-status notes are preserved. A real-PDF regeneration in a
temporary copy retained all 49 Senegal links and every other-country field.

All five second-round perspectives approve the fixes. Fast checks pass
(25 package checks; 1535 tests, seven skipped) and lint passes (332 tests,
ten skipped). The forge review records the final full-suite result.
The direct-page exit criterion is still MISSING for 24 identities; author
merge authorization accepts this partial delivery without claiming closure.

## Bounded scout trial

Three scouts cover all 24 unresolved identities: solar/network (7), rural
programmes (7), other agencies/promoters (10). Each has a ceiling of 12 web
tool calls and approximately eight minutes. They return candidate URLs,
source passages, identity evidence, conflicts and unsuccessful routes.

Acceptance uses the existing contract: corroboration must identify the same
project/programme or an explicitly delimited component. Similar names,
capacities or promotional finance offers do not establish identity or finance.
The parent checks novelty against the 260 registered source URLs, reads primary
evidence and archives accepted new material. A failed search stays a dated
search observation. The existing coverage and finance/physical-separation tests
remain the first checks for any proposed canonical updates.

## Managed follow-up rounds

Continue the same open direct-source criterion. Round 2 assigns solar legal and
contract identity, ASER village/procurement records and ANER original dossiers
to three read-only scouts. The parent verifies primary passages and searches
OMVG STEP and Senelec charging procurement. Round 3 follows only concrete
identifiers or alternate primary repositories learned from round 2. Searches
stop when distinct routes repeat without new identifiers; absence remains a
dated observation, not evidence that a proposal was abandoned.

First tests are the existing 43-identity coverage, direct-source linkage, solar
proposal and PUELEC component/finance separation checks. Any promoted physical
or financial milestone gets a source-specific failing regression before data
integration. Evidence-only rejected leads need no implementation-mirroring test.
Record accepted and rejected matches, exact locators, retrieval outcomes and
remaining document needs. Keep the ticket open unless its literal criterion
is met; public enquiries to institutions are outside this research authorization.


Managed-rounds evidence is consolidated in
`docs/jetp-senegal-managed-rounds-2026-09-13.md` and the historical capture
appendix. The revised charging identity regression protects provisional
matching; the initially proposed preparation event was removed after review.
The BOAD approved loan is preserved as context because neither ledger scope
admits an unjoined, unattributed loan. Coverage remains 20 collected,
20 central-only and 3 blocked; the direct-source exit criterion stays open.


The document-led follow-up supersedes the preceding current-coverage figure:
21 collected, 19 central-only and 3 blocked. See
`docs/jetp-senegal-document-followup-2026-09-13.md` and
`docs/jetp-senegal-document-requests/README.md`. The ANER identity regression
failed before integration. Independent source review accepted the exact
institutional-project match while retaining the conditional budget and objective
outputs as planning evidence. Financial and physical event tables are unchanged.
Six institutional requests are complete and independently reviewed, with an
explicit unsent register. The direct-source exit criterion remains open.
